    <string name="info_message">PermHub shows what your apps are allowed to do, in one place. It has no Internet permission and no ads or analytics, so it cannot send your app list anywhere.\n\nAndroid does not let one app change the permissions of another. PermHub opens the right Android settings page, and you make the change there.\n\nFlags come from simple rules. A flag means an app is worth a look, not that it is malicious. No flag does not mean an app is safe: PermHub only checks the permissions and access it lists.\n\nPermHub only sees the current profile. A work profile needs its own copy.</string>
